      { q: 'What are the key factors influencing the gold price in the market?', a: 'Gold prices are influenced by supply and demand dynamics, geopolitical uncertainty, interest rates, the global economic climate, and the strength of the US dollar. Watching these drivers helps traders anticipate potential price movements.' },
      { q: 'How can I start trading gold with Orion Capital?', a: 'Simply register an account, complete the verification process, make your first deposit, and choose gold as your instrument. You can practise risk-free on a demo account before trading with real money.' },
      { q: 'What are the differences between trading gold CFDs, futures, and options?', a: 'CFDs let you speculate on gold price changes without an expiry commitment, while futures and options are standardised contracts with set expiries and predetermined prices. CFDs are generally simpler for beginners; futures and options suit advanced hedging and speculation strategies.' },
